# Authoring a skill or a fact

Follow the `bbs-claude-md-forge` skill and `docs/MAINTAINER-GUIDE.md`. Stance:

- **One home per fact.** A fact restated in a second file goes stale in one of them. Point
  at the system of record; never re-key it. Per-customer variation is a **profile inside** a
  skill, not a sibling skill that competes on its description.
- **Description carries what + when, under 1024 characters.** It is the routing signal and
  the only text loaded before the skill triggers, so a "When to use" section in the body is
  wasted. Past the limit the "do NOT use for" clause drops silently. Quote a `description:`
  containing a colon, or use a `>-` block scalar, or the skill never loads.
- **Progressive disclosure.** Keep `SKILL.md` to the core workflow; move detail into
  `references/`, one level deep; give any reference over 100 lines a table of contents.
- **Counter-example awareness.** Prose that names a bad value in order to warn about it is
  correct content — keep the qualifying phrase next to the value so `check_marketplace.py`
  reads it as a warning, not a defect.
- **Portable paths only** (`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`, `$SKILL_DIR`), and **model IDs read from
  `models.json`**, never hand-typed.
- **Prove it.** `python3 scripts/check_marketplace.py` exits 0 before you call it done.

